  "rationale": "A valid attack sequence is phish_workstation → pivot_internal → auth_appserver → kerberoast_dc → auth_dc → escalate_dc → dump_dbadmin_dc → auth_db → escalate_db → exfiltrate_db. Phishing grants foothold_workstation and stolen_user, enabling the internal pivot because segmented is not deployed. Appserver access enables theft of stolen_admin, and mfa_admin is not deployed, permitting domain-controller access and escalation to admin_dc. The attacker then obtains stolen_dbadmin. Although mfa_dbadmin is deployed, auth_db explicitly permits access when admin_dc is true. Database escalation and exfiltration therefore remain reachable. The deployed fileserver patch does not block this path."
